  "raw_meta_yaml": "context:\n  version: \"0.3.39\"\n\npackage:\n  name: picamera2\n  version: ${{ version }}\n\nsource:\n  - url: https://pypi.org/packages/source/p/picamera2/picamera2-${{ version }}.tar.gz\n    sha256: 63edb7898b6b652711b5fc1a2f3d6e075b3f884b2b5e40b05037dbe67a1e49f4\n\nbuild:\n  number: 1\n  script: ${{ PYTHON }} -m pip install . -vv --no-deps --no-build-isolation\n  noarch: python\n\nrequirements:\n  host:\n    - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n    - pip\n    - setuptools >=64\n  run:\n    - python >=${{ python_min }}\n    # libcamera 0.x breaks API/ABI every minor release and its Python bindings\n    # are explicitly unstable, so allow only the minors tested on hardware\n    # (Pi 5 + Camera Module 3, picam2_check.py from conda-forge/libcamera-feedstock#31).\n    - libcamera >=0.7,<0.9\n    - pidng\n    - av\n    - jsonschema\n    - pykms\n    - python-libarchive-c\n    - numpy\n    - piexif\n    - pillow\n    - simplejpeg\n    - tqdm\n    - py-videodev2\n    - openexr-python\n    - __linux\n\ntests:\n  - python:\n      imports:\n        - picamera2\n      # piexif from conda-forge ships wheel tags pip rejects:\n      # \"piexif 1.1.3 is not supported on this platform\"\n      pip_check: false\n      python_version:\n        - ${{ python_min }}.*\n        - \"*\"\n  - script: run_test.py\n    requirements:\n      run:\n        - python ${{ python_min }}.*\n\nabout:\n  homepage: https://github.com/RaspberryPi/picamera2\n  repository: https://github.com/RaspberryPi/picamera2\n  documentation: https://datasheets.raspberrypi.com/camera/picamera2-manual.pdf\n  summary: The libcamera-based Python interface to Raspberry Pi cameras, based on the original Picamera library\n  description: |\n    Picamera2 is the libcamera-based replacement for Picamera, which was a\n    Python interface to the Raspberry Pi's legacy camera stack. It provides\n    an easy to use Python API for capturing stills and video, with preview\n    windows, encoders and outputs built on top of libcamera.\n  license: BSD-2-Clause\n  license_file: LICENSE\n\nextra:\n  recipe-maintainers:\n    - carlodri\n",
